<section xml:id="OCES" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Activity Two: Ocean Currents and Their Ecological Significance</title>

  <p> 
    Ocean currents — both surface and deepwater — play critical roles in regulating Earth’s climate and shaping global biomes. 
    Surface currents, such as the Gulf Stream, are primarily driven by wind patterns. 
    Their movement is influenced by differential heating of the atmosphere, the Coriolis effect due to Earth’s rotation, and the configuration of continental landmasses.</p>
  <p> 
    In contrast, deepwater currents are driven by differences in water density, which are affected by temperature and salinity. 
    These currents facilitate the vertical movement of water, bringing nutrient-rich waters from the ocean depths to surface layers where they support marine life. 
    Additionally, deepwater circulation is a key component of global heat transfer, helping to moderate climate across regions.</p>
  <p> 
    In this activity, you will investigate the physical mechanisms that drive deepwater currents and explore their ecological and climatological impacts. </p>
<table>
  <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
    <row left="medium" bottom="medium">
      <cell right="medium" colspan="2"><term>Materials:</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row left="medium" bottom="medium">
      <cell right="medium">Plastic Container</cell>
      <cell right="medium">Chilled Food Coloring</cell>
    </row>
    <row left="medium" bottom="medium">
      <cell right="medium">2 Plastic Cups</cell>
      <cell right="medium">Room Temperature Water</cell>
    </row>
    <row left="medium" bottom="medium">
      <cell right="medium">Ice</cell>
      <cell right="medium">Warm Water</cell>
    </row>
    <row left="medium" bottom="medium">
      <cell right="medium">Sheet of White Paper</cell>
      <cell right="medium"></cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>
</table>


<ol>
  <li>
    <p>Fill the plastic container half-full of room temperature water. Then place the container on top of the white paper.</p>
  <image source="Ac2.jpg" />
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>Fill one of the cups with ice and water and place it close to one end.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>Fill the other cup with warm water and place it at the opposite end. If the cup floats, remove water from the plastic container until it does not float.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>Place one drop of chilled food coloring between the two cups, close to the cup of ice water.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>Observe the movement of the food dye through the water for several minutes.</p>
    <p>Observe the food coloring from:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><p>Above the water</p></li>
      <li><p>At a 45 degree angle</p></li>
      <li><p>From the side of the container</p></li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ol>

